@startuml simplifier_class
title plogic - Simplifier stage

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members

class Orchestrator

class Simplifier {
  +{static} simplify(expression: Expression): Expression
  -{static} erase_grouping(expression: Expression): Expression
  -{static} reduce(expression: Expression): Expression
  -{static} canonicalize(expression: Expression): Expression
  -{static} expand(expression: Expression): Expression
  -{static} weight(expression: Expression): int
  -{static} compare(left: Expression, right: Expression): int
}

abstract class Expression

class Binary

class Unary

class Grouping

class Literal

class Identifier

note bottom of Simplifier
  Pure and total: Expression in, Expression out, no
  errors. Never constructed.

  Four parts:
  0. erase grouping: every Grouping is stripped first;
     the rest never sees it and the output has none.
  1. canonicalize: flatten & / | chains and sort the
     operands in the canonical order (total and
     structural); the AST keeps binary nodes.
  2. reduce: oriented local rewrites, bottom-up, to a
     fixed point; every rule strictly lowers the
     weight W. Rules run in law-table order, and a
     two-operand rule matches any pair of the chain.
  3. expand: laws 4a/4b are tried one at a time and
     kept only if W(candidate) < W(best).

  Conditional and biconditional are eliminated, so
  the output contains only ¬, ∧ and ∨. The result is
  equivalent; no particular normal form is promised.
end note

note right of Expression
  Canonical order, by kind:
  1. constant (F before V)
  2. variable (ASCII code-point, case-sensitive;
     P before p, p before p1)
  3. !x
  4. & chain
  5. | chain
  6. ->, 7. <->
  This order is internal to the Simplifier and shows
  in the simplified formula. The original label keeps
  the written order; with --tabla-simplificada the
  label is the simplified formula and is canonical too.
end note

Orchestrator ..> Simplifier : <<use>>
Simplifier ..> Expression : <<use>>

Binary --|> Expression
Unary --|> Expression
Grouping --|> Expression
Literal --|> Expression
Identifier --|> Expression

@enduml
